$sparkArticles=[
 'style-air-jordan-1'=>['category'=>'Styling Tips','title'=>'How to Style Air Jordan 1','description'=>'Easy outfit formulas that let the iconic Jordan silhouette do the talking.','date'=>'August 24, 2026','image'=>'air-jordan-1-mid.png','content'=>['The Air Jordan 1 works because it balances sport heritage with a clean, everyday shape. Start with straight-leg denim or relaxed trousers so the hem meets the collar without hiding the shoe.','Keep the rest of your palette simple when your pair uses bold color blocking. A neutral tee, overshirt and one accessory in a matching accent creates a considered look without feeling over-styled.','For a softer profile, pair low or mid-top Jordans with cropped pants and visible socks. Comfort matters too: choose your regular size and adjust the lacing rather than sizing up for width.']],
 'everyday-sneakers'=>['category'=>'Buying Guides','title'=>'The Best Sneakers for Everyday Wear','description'=>'What to look for in a pair that can handle commutes, weekends and everything between.','date'=>'August 20, 2026','image'=>'new-balance-530.png','content'=>['The best daily sneaker is the one you forget you are wearing. Look for balanced cushioning, a stable heel and enough toe room for your feet to expand during a long day.','Versatile colors make repeat wear easier, while leather and suede are simple to clean. Mesh feels lighter in hot weather but benefits from a protective spray before regular use.','Rotate between two pairs when possible. Giving cushioning and uppers a day to recover helps both pairs stay comfortable for longer.']],
 'air-force-history'=>['category'=>'Sneaker News','title'=>"Nike Air Force 1: Why It's Still Popular",'description'=>'The design details and cultural staying power behind a true streetwear staple.','date'=>'August 16, 2026','image'=>'nike-air-force-1.png','content'=>['The Air Force 1 began as a basketball shoe and became a streetwear constant because its design is both recognizable and adaptable. The broad panels provide a canvas for color, materials and collaboration.','Its sturdy cupsole and padded collar also make it practical. While trends shift toward slim or chunky shapes, the Air Force 1 sits comfortably between both extremes.','That balance explains its longevity: it can anchor a simple uniform or become the loudest part of an outfit.']],
 'sneaker-trends'=>['category'=>'New Releases','title'=>'Top Sneaker Trends This Year','description'=>'Slim profiles, technical runners and fresh materials defining the current rotation.','date'=>'August 11, 2026','image'=>'adidas-samba.png','content'=>['Low-profile terrace shoes remain strong, especially in suede and gum-sole combinations. At the other end of the spectrum, technical runners bring mesh, metallic overlays and visible cushioning.','Color is becoming more personal. Earth tones make statement shapes wearable, while bright accents revive familiar classics.','The useful takeaway is not to chase every release. Pick the trend that works with the clothes you already own and build from there.']],
 'sneaker-size-guide'=>['category'=>'Buying Guides','title'=>'How to Choose the Right Sneaker Size','description'=>'A practical fitting checklist for more comfortable online sneaker shopping.','date'=>'August 5, 2026','image'=>'nike-air-max-90.png','content'=>['Measure both feet late in the day while wearing the socks you plan to use. Choose for the larger foot and leave roughly a thumb width between your longest toe and the front of the shoe.','Sizing can vary between brands and even between models. Check the product notes and prioritize fit over the number printed on the box.','Your heel should feel secure without pressure, and the widest part of your foot should align with the widest part of the shoe. If either condition fails, try another size or shape.']]
